// Unenrolled User Bypassed MFA via Trusted Network
// A user who has not enrolled in Duo MFA was allowed to authenticate because they were on a trusted network. This represents an MFA coverage gap — an attacker on the trusted network (VPN, compromised workstation, lateral movement) can authenticate as any unenrolled user without MFA. Monitor for unexpected users and push enrollment completion.
// MITRE T1556 - Modify Authentication Process


dataset = duo_mfa_raw
| filter eventType = "authentication"
| filter reason = "allow_unenrolled_user_on_trusted_network"
| alter
    country = access_device_location_country,
    city = access_device_location_city,
    OS = access_device_os,
    browser = access_device_browser
| fields _time, user_name, factor, application_name, access_device_ip, country, city, os, browser, access_device_hostname
| sort desc _time
